WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.610 --> 00:00:07.990
There is a stunning new poll out of the red
state of Georgia in which Democratic presidential

00:00:07.990 --> 00:00:13.369
challenger Joe Biden is winning against Donald
Trump by one point.

00:00:13.369 --> 00:00:19.380
This is absolutely and completely insane and
probably not indicative that Biden is going

00:00:19.380 --> 00:00:20.400
to win Georgia.

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:21.810
And I want to talk about that in a moment.

00:00:21.810 --> 00:00:24.000
There's actually a lot to talk about here.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:28.290
And this is really going to get us into a
discussion of the role of polling going forward

00:00:28.290 --> 00:00:30.990
from now until November 3rd, the last time.

00:00:30.990 --> 00:00:32.640
Let's start in Georgia.

00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:36.800
The last time that a Democratic presidential
candidate won Georgia was 28 years ago.

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:39.050
Was Bill Clinton in 1992.

00:00:39.050 --> 00:00:40.050
It was a squeaker.

00:00:40.050 --> 00:00:46.510
Bill Clinton winning by zero point five percent
of the vote over George H.W. Bush.

00:00:46.510 --> 00:00:51.930
But notice, if you're watching that there
was a third party candidate, Ross Perot, who

00:00:51.930 --> 00:00:54.890
did get 13 percent of the vote in Georgia.

00:00:54.890 --> 00:01:02.219
So the last time that a Democrat won Georgia
without a significant third party candidate

00:01:02.219 --> 00:01:08.290
was 1980, 40 years ago when Jimmy Carter defeated
Ronald Reagan.

00:01:08.290 --> 00:01:11.560
But that was Jimmy Carter's home state.

00:01:11.560 --> 00:01:13.930
So the last time.

00:01:13.930 --> 00:01:15.170
Stick with me here.

00:01:15.170 --> 00:01:21.490
That a Democratic presidential candidate won
Georgia in a two way race when Georgia was

00:01:21.490 --> 00:01:24.820
not their home state was nine.

00:01:24.820 --> 00:01:30.680
1860, when John F. Kennedy defeated Richard
Nixon brutally, 62 to 37.

00:01:30.680 --> 00:01:33.370
That was 60 years ago.

00:01:33.370 --> 00:01:40.000
So when we see a poll today that says Biden's
winning by one in Georgia, to me it's a signal

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:42.920
that it could be a bad November for Trump.

00:01:42.920 --> 00:01:45.770
It's not really a signal that Biden's going
to win Florida.

00:01:45.770 --> 00:01:50.939
The average I'm sorry, Georgia, the average
in Georgia is still Trump winning by one point

00:01:50.939 --> 00:01:51.950
six.

00:01:51.950 --> 00:01:56.980
But the important thing about the latest CBS
News poll, which has Biden plus one, is that

00:01:56.980 --> 00:02:00.880
it's using a likely voter model instead of
a registered voter model.

00:02:00.880 --> 00:02:03.880
And I've talked to you before about the importance
of this.

00:02:03.880 --> 00:02:08.780
If you just survey adults, that's considered
the least accurate because half the country

00:02:08.780 --> 00:02:10.009
doesn't vote.

00:02:10.009 --> 00:02:15.540
If you survey registered voters, it is considered
more accurate because you're at least restricting

00:02:15.540 --> 00:02:18.660
the poll to people who are registered to vote.

00:02:18.660 --> 00:02:22.620
Many registered voters don't vote, but it's
more accurate than just all adults because

00:02:22.620 --> 00:02:26.140
many adults just aren't even registered and
they never vote.

00:02:26.140 --> 00:02:30.630
Likely voter is arguably, if done correctly,
the most accurate.

00:02:30.630 --> 00:02:32.750
And so that's a good thing.

00:02:32.750 --> 00:02:36.930
That's a good sign that as we start to see
registered voter models become likely voter

00:02:36.930 --> 00:02:40.140
models as we close in on November, the polling
should become more accurate.

00:02:40.140 --> 00:02:45.150
That being said, this poll that has Joe Biden
winning by one in Georgia has a three point

00:02:45.150 --> 00:02:46.600
four percent margin of error.

00:02:46.600 --> 00:02:52.690
So what that means is the poll could actually
be in reality.

00:02:52.690 --> 00:02:56.120
Biden is at forty two point six and Trump
is at forty eight point four.

00:02:56.120 --> 00:02:57.880
That's what the margin of error means.

00:02:57.880 --> 00:03:04.660
So this poll, which has Biden plus one, could
actually be Trump plus six and be within the

00:03:04.660 --> 00:03:05.740
margin of error.

00:03:05.740 --> 00:03:12.670
So what that means is we should take nothing
from this other than everybody's got to vote.

00:03:12.670 --> 00:03:16.040
Whether you think your state will be close
or not, you've got to vote.

00:03:16.040 --> 00:03:18.610
I do not believe Trump will win Georgia.

00:03:18.610 --> 00:03:22.370
But if enough polls say it's tight, maybe
Trump has to spend money there.

00:03:22.370 --> 00:03:25.870
Maybe Trump has to campaign to Georgians.

00:03:25.870 --> 00:03:32.489
That's a victory, getting Republicans to have
to spend money in Georgia, in Texas, cetera.

00:03:32.489 --> 00:03:33.629
That's a good thing.

00:03:33.629 --> 00:03:39.540
So the big picture of this sort of battleground
and moderate rates, red state polling, is

00:03:39.540 --> 00:03:44.980
that Trump is now, according to the new polling,
losing by four in North Carolina, losing by

00:03:44.980 --> 00:03:46.209
one in Georgia.

00:03:46.209 --> 00:03:49.370
There is some Texas polling that has Trump
down.

00:03:49.370 --> 00:03:53.350
The meaning of it is this is a really bad
presidency.

00:03:53.350 --> 00:03:58.160
That's the takeaway given the hyper polarized
nature of the country right now.

00:03:58.160 --> 00:04:02.960
When you look at these traditionally red states
and you see that, it looks like it's close.

00:04:02.960 --> 00:04:09.060
That means that there are some partizan right
wingers that are realizing this is so bad

00:04:09.060 --> 00:04:13.930
that I'm at least as of right now, not yet
committed to support Donald Trump.

00:04:13.930 --> 00:04:15.750
You know, Mago will be Magga.

00:04:15.750 --> 00:04:18.029
Trump will still get tens of millions of votes.

00:04:18.029 --> 00:04:20.449
That's an indictment of our country, no doubt.

00:04:20.449 --> 00:04:28.309
But there is actually some reason that is
injecting itself up, embedding itself in the

00:04:28.309 --> 00:04:30.819
brains of some committed right wingers.

00:04:30.819 --> 00:04:32.389
But we can't forgive the ignorance.

00:04:32.389 --> 00:04:37.289
If our population had been better at critical
thinking and had done 10 minutes of actual

00:04:37.289 --> 00:04:39.569
research back in 2016.

00:04:39.569 --> 00:04:42.490
Trump never would have been the nominee and
certainly never would have become president

00:04:42.490 --> 00:04:43.580
of the United States.

00:04:43.580 --> 00:04:49.009
Many of the unnecessary coronavirus deaths
that we've had would not have happened, and

00:04:49.009 --> 00:04:52.460
that number is likely to hit 160000 in the
next day or two.

00:04:52.460 --> 00:04:57.300
So what we want to do here is understand what's
happening so that it doesn't happen again.

00:04:57.300 --> 00:04:58.710
Starting with this November.

00:04:58.710 --> 00:05:00.360
But we can't forget how it happened.

00:05:00.360 --> 00:05:04.330
We can't ignore that it could happen again
and it still might happen again in November

00:05:04.330 --> 00:05:05.330
if we don't vote.

00:05:05.330 --> 00:05:08.389
So to go back to Georgia for a moment.

00:05:08.389 --> 00:05:13.089
It's not just that there's a margin of error
and Trump might actually be winning like that's

00:05:13.089 --> 00:05:15.719
one interpretation would be OK.

00:05:15.719 --> 00:05:16.719
Biden's plus one.

00:05:16.719 --> 00:05:20.469
But you look at the margin of error, could
really be Trump plus six.

00:05:20.469 --> 00:05:22.110
That's that's one part of it.

00:05:22.110 --> 00:05:27.260
The other part of it is when you look at the
history of voter suppression in Georgia, when

00:05:27.260 --> 00:05:32.869
you look at the planned voter suppression
in Georgia, it should give us zero confidence

00:05:32.869 --> 00:05:38.990
that these close states are even going to
have a shot at going our way unless we completely

00:05:38.990 --> 00:05:42.129
overwhelm the voting in November.

00:05:42.129 --> 00:05:44.330
So it's a sad reality.

00:05:44.330 --> 00:05:48.939
There's a lot we're up against right now,
and it includes five or six different ways

00:05:48.939 --> 00:05:52.020
in which Donald Trump is going to try to suppress
the vote.

00:05:52.020 --> 00:05:53.689
We have to accept that and work with it.

00:05:53.689 --> 00:05:59.779
And what that means is so overwhelming voting
turnout and every every election, both sides

00:05:59.779 --> 00:06:00.779
say it.

00:06:00.779 --> 00:06:02.009
Where are sides motivated?

00:06:02.009 --> 00:06:05.689
We're going to have record turnout and very
often, particularly among some voting groups,

00:06:05.689 --> 00:06:07.089
it doesn't happen.

00:06:07.089 --> 00:06:13.729
We actually have to do that to overwhelm Trump,
kneecapping the post office, voter purges,

00:06:13.729 --> 00:06:16.340
limiting vote by mail and on and on and on.

00:06:16.340 --> 00:06:16.409
that's the only way forward.

